    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d677">

                <pb facs="0897" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg801"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore to Mr.
                            Cambon.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: This Government is advised that the
                    Eastern Telegraph Company will at once proceed to restore cable communication
                    between Hongkong and Manila if the United States and Spain will consent to that
                    measure.</p>
                <p>This Government desires such communication to be reopened and, as we have
                    restored Spain to full telegraphic communication with Cuba, it is not supposed
                    that she will object to the reestablishment of cable communication between
                    Hongkong and Manila.</p>
                <p>The Department will be greatly obliged to your excellency if you will be so good
                    as to communicate with the Spanish Government on the subject.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Moore</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
